<div class="values">
  <section class="value">
    <div>
      <h2>Stop paying to find the same problem twice.</h2>
      <p>Doctors run without model inference. Put the checks you already trust first, then spend AI and human review on unfamiliar behavior, architecture, and risk.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="snippet">
      <span class="dim">$</span> npx any-doctor@latest run --all<br />
      <span class="ok">✓</span> 221 files scanned <span class="dim">· local · 0 tokens</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="value">
    <div>
      <h2>Make your codebase's rules executable.</h2>
      <p>A doctor is a JavaScript file with named checks and evidence. Give your agent a real mistake, the correction you want, and innocent examples that must stay quiet.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="snippet">
      <span class="dim">check:</span> abort-signal-required<br />
      <span class="dim">find:</span> request helper without signal<br />
      <span class="dim">skip:</span> unresolved or unrelated calls
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="value">
    <div>
      <h2>Keep the decision, not just the finding.</h2>
      <p>Fix a real problem, or mark intentional code as accepted with a reason. Reviewed findings stay inspectable and return when their evidence or the doctor's meaning changes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="snippet">
      <span class="ok">✓</span> accepted as intended<br />
      <span class="dim">reason:</span> admin-only path<br />
      <span class="dim">view:</span> reviewed findings
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

